CONDITION OF ACCESS & DUAL-LICENSE ARCHITECTURE
================================================================================
Access to, downloading, copying, compiling, executing, or evaluating the
QClearance framework—including its source code, quantum circuits, Oseen–Carleman
Padé-(1,2) stiff ODE operators, three-stage analytical preconditioners,
multiresolution Brickwall VQLS solvers, Heavy-Hex Counterdiabatic QAOA
(HH-CD-QAOA) polypharmacy schedulers, closed-loop Two-Level System (TLS) readout
screening protocols, and curated pharmacokinetic datasets—is governed by a
strict Dual-License model:

  1. FREE FOR STUDENTS & ACADEMIC RESEARCHERS (Section 1):
     Governed by the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (for software, code,
     quantum circuits, and algorithms) and CC BY-NC 4.0 (for curated datasets
     and documentation).

  2. STRICT CORPORATE EXCLUSION & COMMERCIAL LICENSE (Section 2):
     All for-profit corporations, commercial laboratories, pharmaceutical/biotech
     companies, clinical software vendors, and quantum hardware/cloud providers
     are strictly excluded from Section 1 and require an executed commercial
     license agreement with the Author even for internal R&D, evaluation, or
     hardware benchmarking.

